{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/627250-new-foray-into-wod-and-hunter-story-help-request","id":627250,"title":"New foray into WoD and Hunter, Story help request","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-14T22:12:09-07:00","id":627250,"title":"New foray into WoD and Hunter, Story help request","content":"Hey everyone, Im relatively new to WoD and my co-workers want to start a gaming night and i got slated to run it. So i was wondering if i could get a little bit of help. Most people have little to no knowledge in the setting. My knowledge is mostly from the oWoD, I used to play VTeS and played both of the VtM PC games. So i have a decent understand but i know they revamped clans and all that with the nWoD.<br /> <br /> Anyway, so i decided to base my game off of my hometown. Partly because i can think of more details to incorporate and also because i see a lot of potential to make it more occult based. Newark Ohio, a medium size town just 30 min outside of Columbus, is home to the Hopewell Indian Earthworks. Basically a network of mounds that relate to some unknown moon based worship. Just south of Newark is Buckeye Lake. A man made lake previously a swamp back in the 1700s or so. In the last year they have worried about possible catastrophic dam failure so they lowered the lakes water level. Then just outside of Newark is a odd building shaped just like a giant basket. No joke (<a href=\"http://1.bp.blogspot.com/-PVmREfv8sDo/UGaLPJ4z36I/AAAAAAAAAgI/rRh31sJRLMQ/s1600/i3.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://1.bp.blogspot.com/-PVmREfv8sD...Q/s1600/i3.jpg</a>)<br /> <br /> So here is the concept i have so far but i could use a little help fluffing out the story and baddies. Early on i was going to run both of the pre-made chapters by WW to get the players a feel for the system and kinda stall a bit so i can work on the story. I was going to start them off investigating in Columbus and then move to Newark. I was thinking of a few different groups of baddies. Starting with Buckeye Lake, i was thinking an amphibian race were the main reason the lake was formed was to bury them. Residents were having people go missing because of these monsters. Now that the water level has lowered, they have reawakened. Next i was thinking a werewolf biker gang based out of the burial mounds. They use it as a loci (if im right on the term) but also try to resume some of the moon worship. Maybe I might make a special lunar occurrence during their investigation that might make them super strong/more feral. I was thinking of keeping the WWs a little more neutral. Next a self styled vampire prince of Newark trying to gain more power by using a local gang. Then maybe a small group of vampires who just live off of the small college branch in town. Lastly the basket might be a group of mages/spirits/monsters trying to force open another loci to break the hold away from the WWs.<br /> <br /> So here are my questions<br /> 1)For the swamp monsters, i was thinking of using frog like humanoids. They may be a bit violent in nature, killing people who are too close. But to tie into the burial mounds, should they be holding onto some kind of relic for some reason? What relic would they have and why would it relate to the mounds? Specifically with the fact that it was native american based?<br /> 2) For these new creatures, are there rules for creating your own monsters? If so what book pgs?<br /> 3) With the basket plot hook, who would be most logical and does the concept i have in mind sound decent at all?<br /> 4) For Hunter, should i allow them into any conspiracy or limit them or kinda crate their own with benefits. I just dont want to make them a part of some big national org. I want them to feel small but maybe have a little backing. Like maybe most of the groups are based out of Columbus but they are far enough away to limit immediate aid.<br /> <br /> Well thanks for listening and even more thanks for any advice. Any bit helps because i just dont know what fits just yet in the setting.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7312-coop_dh","name":"Coop_DH","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T22:58:02-07:00","id":627289,"title":"","content":"You sound like you've got a great handle on it already. It helps that Hunter is less invested in sticking closely to the lore of the other gamelines, with hunters usually in positions where they don't get the full picture of what's going on, making it easy to play with exception cases and weird miscellaneous phenomena like your frogmans. In terms of differences from the cWoD, mostly the nWoD is less stylistically exaggerated in terms of being grittier and gargoylier than the real world, and has a Fortean undercurrent to it that stresses mystery and the uncanny. There's a lot more present in terms of weird stuff that doesn't belong and is &quot;just there,&quot; rather than tying in to a grand defined mythos. The nWoD is a deep, foggy place where investigation raises more questions than it answers.<br /> <br /> Rules for putting monsters together can be found in the Storytelling chapter under Dread Powers, pp. 276-283. Various Hunter supplement books often have a few more, especially Mortal Remains, which covers a lot of conceptual ground as it serves as a hunter's eye view of five other gamelines. There's not really a point-buy system or relative costs for different combinations of Dread Powers, so it's still very salt-to-taste, but they cover things like driving people crazy, inhuman claws, or revealing your true monstrous form.<br /> <br /> You should definitely make your players adhere to a group concept they (and you) can all agree on before you design individual characters. Picking a compact or conspiracy isn't like picking a clan and then all showing up in the same society as peers. And remember, not having any compact or conspiracy is perfectly legit; that's what the Hunter corebook refers to as &quot;tier one&quot; play. Having your characters all part of the same organization is probably ideal, but you can certainly make a combination work as long as you have a unifying vision of what ties the cell together conceptually and what keeps them together cooperatively. If you want an action-heavy game, you might have a Union cell that represents most of the local Union power, but that can ask for help from neighboring areas now and then; or you could have a coalition of shitkickers from different organizations which each have a vested interest in keeping the Vigil over Newark. If you want an investigative game, you could be a Network Zero ghost-hunting team looking to get enough hard evidence to shine their way to a TV deal and wow the world, or you could be the local eggheads of Newark's compacts, used to running into each other, who have become friends and help each other with their respective research getting to the bottom of these mysteries.<br /> <br /> If the burial mounds are associated with practices of moon worship, you might have an unusual concentration of Wolf-Blooded in their vicinity: people who have been blessed and cursed by the touch of Mother Moon in some manner, and who sometimes then become full-fledged werewolves. Maybe the biker pack's rites have caused this rate to rise after having laid long dormant, but the new werewolves don't really buy into the bikers' weird moon religion, Shadow Realm or no Shadow Realm. Maybe it might be possible to play the different werewolves against one another, or even form allies amongst them.<br /> <br /> The big basket is great and I want to thank you just for sharing it. It's hard to use in a deadly serious tone, but if you don't mind cutting your horror with a bit of humor (and Lord knows I don't mind it), it might be an example of the uncanny infrastructure of the God-Machine, the antagonist of Demon: the Descent, whose cults, servants and uncaring angels are known to put together weird fusions of creepy shadow symbolism and modern everyday business, because it knows just the right weird juxtaposition at just the right time can achieve some bizarre occult effect. Perhaps the basket is a nexus for a network of energy that creates backdoor passages and secret bases linking together all of the malls and department stores in Newark, which the God-Machine's people then use for whatever other creepy things they're doing \u2013 kidnapping and reprogramming people, shipping in reptoid footsoldiers, storing all of Ohio's missing left socks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T16:52:15-07:00","id":629201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/627250-new-foray-into-wod-and-hunter-story-help-request?p=627289#post627289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big basket is great and I want to thank you just for sharing it. It's hard to use in a deadly serious tone, but if you don't mind cutting your horror with a bit of humor (and Lord knows I don't mind it), it might be an example of the uncanny infrastructure of the God-Machine, the antagonist of Demon: the Descent, whose cults, servants and uncaring angels are known to put together weird fusions of creepy shadow symbolism and modern everyday business, because it knows just the right weird juxtaposition at just the right time can achieve some bizarre occult effect. Perhaps the basket is a nexus for a network of energy that creates backdoor passages and secret bases linking together all of the malls and department stores in Newark, which the God-Machine's people then use for whatever other creepy things they're doing \u2013 kidnapping and reprogramming people, shipping in reptoid footsoldiers, storing all of Ohio's missing left socks.</div> </div> </div> </div> Let me make a suggestion: The basket is NOT God-Machine Infrastructure, (or at least not anymore) but rather something a local group (Agency? I'm unfamiliar with D:tD terminology) of Unchained are attempting to use as a way to reach Hell...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}